<article class="env-definition" id="04TH">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/04TH">Definition <span data-tag="04TH">94.16.4</span>.</a> Let $S$ be a scheme. Let $B$ be an algebraic space over $S$. Let $(U, R, s, t, c)$ be a groupoid in algebraic spaces over $B$. We say $(U, R, s, t, c)$ is a <em>smooth groupoid</em><a class="footnotemark" href="#a0001656749" id="a0001656749-mark"><sup>1</sup></a> if $s, t : R \to U$ are smooth morphisms of algebraic spaces. </p>
</article>